#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;border-left-width:1pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:117pt;border-top-color:#000000;border-bottom-style:solid"><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Fully visible text and critical visual subject area</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Any detected text bounding box intersecting an exclusion polygon triggers an automatic geometry layout violation.</span></p><h3 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Transcript Matching and Caption Timing Alignment</span></h3><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The post-render caption verification pipeline performs two distinct audits: content fidelity and temporal pacing.</span></p><ul class="lst-kix_list_8-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Content Fidelity via String Distance: Extracted OCR tokens within the caption bounding area are concatenated and compared against the intended script segment using normalized Levenshtein distance: \text{Similarity}(S_{\text{OCR}}, S_{\text{Script}}) = 1 - \frac{\text{Levenshtein}(S_{\text{OCR}}, S_{\text{Script}})}{\max(\vert{}S_{\text{OCR}}\vert{}, \vert{}S_{\text{Script}}\vert{})} A similarity score below 0.88 (accounting for minor OCR character confusion on stylized fonts) flags an invalid caption render (e.g., dropped words, truncation, or character encoding failure like "???").</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Temporal Timing Verification via WhisperX Forced Alignment: While standard Whisper transcription generates coarse, utterance-level timestamps interpolated across 30-second audio windows, WhisperX performs a secondary phoneme-level forced alignment pass using Wav2Vec2 and Dynamic Time Warping (DTW). This aligns the true audio speech boundaries down to sub-100 millisecond precision. The post-render caption validator extracts the display entry timestamp (t_{\text{display\_start}}) and exit timestamp (t_{\text{display\_end}}) of the burned-in graphic and compares them to the true acoustic speech boundaries (t_{\text{audio\_start}}, t_{\text{audio\_end}}):</span></li></ul><ul class="lst-kix_list_9-1 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:60pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Subtitle Lead: t_{\text{display\_start}} &lt; t_{\text{audio\_start}} - 200\text{ ms} (caption appears noticeably before speech begins).</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:60pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Subtitle Lag: t_{\text{display\_start}} &gt; t_{\text{audio\_start}} + 250\text{ ms} (speech begins noticeably before caption appears).</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:60pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Early Disappearance: t_{\text{display\_end}} &lt; t_{\text{audio\_end}} - 300\text{ ms} (caption vanishes while dialogue continues).</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:60pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Reading Speed Compliance: Display duration must support human reading speed. Reading rate is calculated as: R = \frac{\text{Character Count}}{t_{\text{displa[span_18](start_span)[span_18](end_span)[span_25](start_span)[span_25](end_span)y\_end}} - t_{\text{display\_start}}} Rates exceeding 21\text{ characters per second} (CPS) violate accessibility standards and are flagged as unreadable.</span></li></ul><h2 style="padding-top:11.2pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">7. Semantic and Multimodal AI QA Stack</span></h2><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Deterministic signal analyzers cannot determine whether an image of an apple was rendered when the script called for an orange, or if a generated visual contradicts the voiceover narrative. Semantic verification requires multimodal foundation models, but their deployment must be strictly constrained by mathematical trust boundaries.</span></p><h3 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The Semantic Scene Contract</span></h3><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Every video project managed by Hermes compiles a deterministic, machine-readable JSON scene contract before rendering begins. This contract serves as the ground-truth specification against which the visual output is audited:</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Courier&quot;;font-style:normal">{<br> &nbsp;"scene_id": "scene_004",<br> &nbsp;"timecode_range": ["00:00:12.500", "00:00:16.200"],<br> &nbsp;"frame_range": [375, 486],<br> &nbsp;"expected_elements": {<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;"primary_subject": "vintage steam locomotive",<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;"background_environment": "foggy mountain pass",<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;"required_text": "THE STEAM AGE",<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;"prohibited_elements": ["modern automobiles", "aircraft", "distorted text"],<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;"mood_tone": "cinematic historical"<br> &nbsp;}<br>}<br></span></p><h3 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Multimodal Trust Boundaries and Verification Hierarchy</span></h3><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">To eliminate model hallucination and preserve determinism, semantic verification is partitioned into three hierarchical tiers:</span></p><table style="border-spacing:0;border-collapse:collapse;margin-right:auto"><thead><tr style="height:0pt"><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;bor