der-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:78pt;border-top-color:#000000;border-bottom-style:solid"><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">High (Hardcoded deterministic passes)</span></p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;border-left-width:1pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:78pt;border-top-color:#000000;border-bottom-style:solid"><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">High (Fully isolated internal process)</span></p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;border-left-width:1pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:78pt;border-top-color:#000000;border-bottom-style:solid"><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">RECOMMENDED PRODUCTION PATH. Custom FastMCP server purpose-built for QA.</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Community MCP servers provide general media editing wrappers but lack specialized verification primitives (e.g., parsing EBU R128 logs, checking safe-zone intersections, or computing Laplacian blur). The production engine must implement a purpose-built FastMCP QA Server (hermes-media-qc) exposing structured tools (run_technical_qc, verify_captions, compile_repair_intent) directly to Hermes.</span></p><h2 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">14. Performance Considerations and Hardware Acceleration</span></h2><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Automated QA must operate at high throughput to avoid becoming the primary bottleneck in the publishing pipeline. Hardware acceleration must be applied strategically to balance CPU and GPU workloads.</span></p><h3 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Hardware-Specific Throughput Characteristics</span></h3><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The verification pipeline distributes workloads across compute subsystems based on processing profiles:</span></p><ul class="lst-kix_list_f-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Container &amp; Metadata Ingest (FFprobe / MediaInfo): Pure I/O and container atom parsing. Execution time: 50\text{ ms} - 150\text{ ms} on standard NVMe SSDs. Pure CPU execution.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Baseband Signal Pass (FFmpeg Null Decode): Decoding full-raster 4K/1080p video while running simultaneous audio/video filtergraphs. On an AMD EPYC 16-core CPU, software decoding runs at 4.5\times - 8\times real-time. Utilizing hardware-accelerated decoding via NVIDIA NVDEC (ffmpeg -hwaccel cuda -hwaccel_output_format cuda -i input.mp4 ...) elevates throughput to 22\times - 35\times real-time, completing a 10-minute video audit in under 20 seconds.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Computer Vision Heuristics (OpenCV Laplacian / Histograms): Vectorized frame operations executed in Python/NumPy. Processing a 1080p frame takes 3.5\text{ ms} on a modern CPU core (&gt; 280\text{ fps}). GPU acceleration (via OpenCV CUDA or PyTorch tensors) reduces this to &lt; 0.8\text{ ms} per frame, but PCI-e bus transfer overhead makes batch CPU processing more cost-effective for downscaled frames (1280 \times 720).</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">OCR Extraction (PaddleOCR v4): Inference time per frame is heavily hardware-dependent. On a multi-threaded CPU, text detection and recognition require 180\text{ ms} - 320\text{ ms} per frame. Deploying PaddleOCR via TensorRT or ONNX Runtime on an NVIDIA RTX 4090 or A4000 reduces inference to 18\text{ ms} - 35\text{ ms} per frame. For a 10-minute video sampled at 3 frames per shot (~60 shots = 180 frames), total GPU OCR processing completes in \approx 4.5\text{ seconds}.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Multimodal Semantic Validation (SigLIP &amp; Qwen2.5-VL): Vector embedding generation via SigLIP-SO400M takes \approx 12\text{ ms} per image on GPU. Running Qwen2.5-VL-7B through vLLM takes \approx 450\text{ ms} - 900\text{ ms} per query. Restricting VLM evaluation to the 5 to 10 critical transition scenes keeps overall neural semantic evaluation under 8 seconds.</span></li></ul><h3 style="padding-top:12pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Acceleration Strategy Recommendation</span></h3><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">To achieve an end-to-end QA execution latency of under 45 seconds on a 10-minute master render:</span></p><ul class="lst-kix_list_10-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Pin FFmpeg decoding to hardware decoders (NVDEC) where available, piping uncompressed frame buffers directly into downstream filter chains.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Execute OpenCV blur, exposure, and frame differencing across downscaled luma buffers (1280 \times 720 resolution).</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Dedicate GPU resources exclusively to high-value inference tasks: TensorRT-accelerated PaddleOCR, WhisperX Wav2Vec2 phoneme alignment, and vLLM-hosted Qwen2.5-VL.</span></li></ul><h2 style="padding-top:11.2pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">15. Licensing, Platform Terms, and Data Governance</span></h2><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">An autonomous production engine must operate with zero legal ambiguity regarding software licenses, commercial distribution rights, and data privacy.</span></p><h3 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Software License Analysis</span></h3><ul class="lst-kix_list_11-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">FFmpeg: Licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License (LGPL) version 2.1+ by default, but transitions to the GNU General Public License (GPL) version 2.0+ if compiled with --enable-gpl (required for certain optimized decoders, x264, or postproc filters). Commercial automated pipelines must run FFmpeg as an external, decoupled command-line subprocess rather than linking directly to libavcodec/libavformat shared libraries within proprietary source code. This satisfies LGPL/GPL dynamic isolation boundaries.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">MediaInfo &amp; MediaConch: Licensed under the BSD 2-Clause license (MediaInfoLib) and GPLv3+ (MediaConch). Fully compatible with commercial automation when invoked via CLI/JSON interfaces.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">OpenCV: Licensed under the Apache 2.0 License. Permissive for enterprise commercial deployment without copyleft contamination.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">PaddleOCR: Licensed under the Apache 2.0 License. Safe for commercial production and private container deployment.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span>WhisperX &amp; Whisper: OpenAI Whisper is MIT-licensed. WhisperX is BSD-4 Clause licensed. However, if PyAnnote.audio is incorporated for speaker diarization, PyAnnote enforces a custom license requiring explicit Hugging Face gated access tokens and restrictions on commercial derivative training. For post-render caption QA, the pipeline utilizes </span><span style="font-style:italic">only</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;the forced phoneme aligner (Wav2Vec2), completely bypassing PyAnnote diarization dependencies to maintain an unencumbered permissive license model.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Remotion: Governed by the Remotion Company License. Free for individuals and entities with under 3 employees, but requires an active commercial enterprise license for larger organizations rendering programmatic video at scale.</span></li></ul><h3 style="padding-top:12pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Multimodal Models and Data Privacy Considerations</span></h3><ul class="lst-kix_list_12-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Model Weight Licensing: Qwen2.5-VL is released under the Apache 2.0 license, permitting unrestricted local commercial inference. Googleâ€™s SigLIP models are released under Apache 2.0.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Data Privacy &amp; Zero Egress: By deploying all verification analyzers locally (on dedicated GPU worker nodes or on-premise clusters), no video assets, transcripts, voice stems, or visual frames are transmitted to third-party hosted APIs (such as OpenAI, Anthropic, or cloud QA vendors). This eliminates per-minute API fees, insulates the pipeline against external API rate limits, and protects proprietary media assets prior to scheduled publication.</span></li></ul><h2 style="padding-top:11.2pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">16. Genuine Custom-Build Gaps</span></h2><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Standard open-source packages excel at isolated tasks (FFmpeg decodes bitstreams, OpenCV processes matrices, PaddleOCR reads text, WhisperX extracts phonemes). However, researching the landscape reveals that no unified, open-source tool natively bridges these systems into an autonomous verification and remediation engine for programmatic video.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The following architectural components represent genuine custom-build requirements:</span></p><ul class="lst-kix_list_13-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Unified Multimodal QA Orchestrator (hermes-qa-engine): An asynchronous Python/Rust orchestration runtime that manages the layered execution pipeline: firing FFmpeg null decoders, aggregating OpenCV frame metrics, batching keyframes into TensorRT-PaddleOCR, and querying local VLMs under strict timeout and error-handling budgets.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Cross-Tool Evidence Normalizer: An analytical parser that intercepts unstructured standard error logs (from FFmpeg, MediaInfo, and filter outputs) and maps them into the standardized, typed JSON finding schema defined in Section 10.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Subtitle Timing Drift Correlator: A specialized diff engine that reconciles WhisperX phoneme timestamp intervals with PaddleOCR bounding box appearances across the video timeline, computing programmatic lead, lag, and reading velocity metrics.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Failure Fingerprint and Retry Budget Engine: A stateful tracking layer integrated with SQLite that hashes incoming defects, evaluates recurring failure signatures, decrements retry budgets per scene, and enforces deterministic escalation.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Surgical Repair Intent Compiler: A translation engine that converts temporal findings ([t_1, t_2]) into concrete worker actions: calculating exact Remotion frame numbers (--frames), synthesizing patch configs, invoking render workers, and executing the lossless FFmpeg concat demuxer assembly.</span></li></ul><h2 style="padding-top:11.2pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">17. Targeted Validation Queue</span></h2><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">To move this architectural specification into production implementation, engineering items must be systematically validated across four functional domains:</span></p><h3 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Architecture Decisions</span></h3><ul class="lst-kix_list_14-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Concat Splicing GOP Alignment: Validate whether Remotion rendered patches can be losslessly spliced into H.264 master containers without re-encoding adjacent scenes, or if Remotion must be forced to output closed-GOP keyframes at the exact splice boundaries (--gop 1 or fixed GOP length).</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Safe-Zone Mask Definition: Finalize and codify the pixel coordinate polygon for YouTube Shorts UI occlusion across mobile viewports (iOS vs Android button placement differences).</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Decoupled Audio Remixing: Determine whether audio loudness and clipping repairs should bypass Remotion entirely by re-mixing audio stems via FFmpeg/Sox and muxing the new audio track directly into the master container (-c:v copy -c:a aac) in sub-second execution.</span></li></ul><h3 style="padding-top:12pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Research Findings and Empirical Benchmarks</span></h3><ul class="lst-kix_list_15-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Decode Explosion Reliability: Verify across corrupt test files that ffmpeg -v error -err_detect explode -xerror -i input.mp4 -f null - reliably catches all simulated macroblock dropouts and packet truncations across both H.264 (AVC) and H.265 (HEVC) streams.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">WhisperX Timing Precision: Benchmark the sub-100ms accuracy claim of WhisperX phoneme alignment on synthetic and human speech audio tracks containing background music ducking.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">PaddleOCR vs Scene Complexity: Quantify PaddleOCR v4 text detection recall on stylized kinetic typography featuring drop shadows, glows, and animated character scales.</span></li></ul><h3 style="padding-top:12pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Hypotheses and Heuristic Thresholds</span></h3><ul class="lst-kix_list_16-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Laplacian Blur Threshold Calibration: Test the hypothesis that a Laplacian variance threshold of \text{Var}(\nabla^2 I) &lt; 100.0 correctly separates corrupt/blurry frames from intentional soft-focus background art.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">SigLIP Semantic Threshold: Validate whether a SigLIP cosine similarity threshold of S_C \ge 0.28 provides sufficient discriminative power to flag incorrect stock footage insertions without false-positive rejections.</span></li></ul><h3 style="padding-top:12pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Unresolved Questions and Implementation Candidates</span></h3><ul class="lst-kix_list_17-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Hardware-Accelerated Filtergraphs: Benchmark whether executing FFmpeg's ebur128 and blackdetect directly within CUDA hardware memory (-hwaccel cuda) provides significant throughput gains compared to decoding to system RAM and filtering on CPU.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">FastMCP Python Packaging: Evaluate whether the custom QA orchestrator should be packaged as a FastMCP server or as a native gRPC service for lower-overhead IPC with Hermes.</span></li></ul><h2 style="padding-top:11.2pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">18. Recommended Architecture</span></h2><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The Autonomous Video QA, Verification, Publishability Gate, and Surgical Repair Ecosystem is structured as a sequential pipeline coordinated by the master director. The pipeline is designed so that early, low-cost deterministic checks eliminate invalid files before expensive, high-level multimodal models are ever invoked.</span></p><h3 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Pipeline Execution Architecture</span></h3><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The operational flow progresses through seven distinct processing phases:</span></p><ol class="lst-kix_list_18-0 start" start="1" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Stage 0: Ingest &amp; Container Guard (FFprobe / MediaInfo). Triggers immediately upon completion of video rendering. Extracts container atoms, stream counts, duration deltas, codecs, pixel formats, and color metadata. Enforces Stage 0 Gate: if the container is truncated, missing an audio stream, or missing a moov atom, the run aborts immediately with a BLOCK status.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Stage 1: Deterministic Bitstream &amp; Signal Scan (FFmpeg Null Decoder). Executes ffmpeg -v error -err_detect explode -xerror -i file.mp4 -f null - with parallel audio/video filtergraphs. Simultaneously scans for baseband black frames (blackdetect), frozen frames (freezedetect), baseband silence (silencedetect), audio clipping (astats), and integrated loudness (ebur128). Emits structured timecode logs for any baseband signal anomaly.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Stage 2: Scene Segmentation &amp; Keyframe Extraction (PySceneDetect). Partitions the video into discrete shot intervals using the ContentDetector algorithm. Extracts three representative frames per shot: entry (t_{10\%}), midpoint (t_{50\%}), and exit (t_{90\%}). Maps each shot to its corresponding record in the Hermes Scene Contract manifest.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Stage 3: Spatial, Typography &amp; Layout Audit (OpenCV + PaddleOCR). Processes midpoint frames through OpenCV for Laplacian blur variance and luminance histogram analysis. Executes TensorRT-accelerated PaddleOCR to extract burned-in typography and caption text. Performs geometric intersection tests between text bounding boxes and the YouTube Shorts UI occlusion mask. Runs Levenshtein string distance checks comparing extracted text against the scene contract script.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Stage 4: Multimodal Semantic &amp; Caption Timing Verification (SigLIP / WhisperX / Qwen2.5-VL). Computes SigLIP vector embeddings for sampled frames and evaluates cosine similarity against expected scene prompts. Executes WhisperX forced alignment on the audio stream and calculates caption lead, lag, and display duration metrics. If SigLIP scores indicate ambiguity (0.22 \le S_C &lt; 0.30), queries local Qwen2.5-VL-7B via vLLM with grammar-constrained JSON schemas to confirm subject and context alignment.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Stage 5: Publishability Gate &amp; Decision Evaluation. Ingests findings from Stages 0 through 4 into the centralized gate engine. Evaluates all findings against the Policy Threshold Table (Section 9). If zero BLOCK findings exist: emits overall_status: "PASSED" and unlocks the distribution pipeline. If one or more BLOCK findings exist: emits overall_status: "FAILED[span_70](start_span)[span_70](end_span)", halts release, and routes the report to the Repair Compiler.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Stage 6: Surgical Remediation Loop. The Repair Compiler hashes defect signatures into failure fingerprints and checks the SQLite retry budget. If the retry budget is valid: compiles a Repair Intent targeting the failed scene interval [f_{\text{start}}, f_{\text{end}}]. For visual/text defects: dispatches Remotion CLI with --frames=&lt;start&gt;-&lt;end&gt; to render an isolated replacement segment. For audio loudness/clipping defects: re-levels audio stems and re-muxes the audio container track directly. Audits the newly rendered segment through an isolated QA pass. Slices the patch into the master container using the FFmpeg concat demuxer (-c copy) and executes boundary verification. If the retry budget is exhausted: updates state to ESCALATE_TO_HERMES_DIRECTOR for autonomous script revision or human intervention.</span></li></ol><h3 style="padding-top:12pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Architectural Component Classification</span></h3><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The verification and remediation components occupy distinct functional roles within the system:</span></p><table style="border-spacing:0;border-collapse:collapse;margin-right:auto"><thead><tr style="height:0pt"><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;border-left-width:1pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:117pt;border-top-color:#000000;border-bottom-style:solid"><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">System Component</span></p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;border-left-width:1pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:117pt;border-top-color:#000000;border-bottom-style:solid"><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Architectural Role</span></p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1